Four classes carry almost all of empirical work: numeric (numbers), character (text), logical (TRUE/FALSE), and Date. A vector holds exactly one of them. That constraint sets up the next section.

The missing spring, measured
A bar chart finds the hole. Measuring it takes a chain you can now read:






Write down the twelve counts this should print. The evidence: the count() above says the regulatory series has 301 rows. A full month has 28 to 31 days. A count plot of this series shows ten tall bars, April near two days, May near one. Your twelve numbers must sum to 301.




year &lt;- pm |&gt;
  filter(POC == 1, AQS.Parameter.Code == 88101) |&gt;
  mutate(month = factor(format(date, "%b"), levels = month.abb))

